  "id": "baconian-method",
  "term": "Baconian method",
  "definition": "The Baconian method is a way of inquiry that starts with many particular observations and builds broader ideas only from what comparison of those cases supports. In its stricter historical sense, it refers to Francis Bacon’s form of induction, which tries to isolate what is essential to a phenomenon by excluding features that do not consistently appear with it.",
